### Managed by Ansible — roles/splunk-es. Do not edit on the host.
#
# Overrides Splunk_TA_microsoft_sysmon so Sysmon events are actually usable.
#
# ss-pp-stacked 2026-09-04: 623,448 Sysmon events were indexed with NOT ONE
# extracted field. EventCode, process, src -- all empty, while the raw XML sat
# there intact. ES dashboards fed by Sysmon were empty and hunt workstations
# could not search process ancestry. Every other check passed throughout.
#
# TWO INDEPENDENT FAULTS, both measured on the range.
#
# 1. THE RENAME TARGET IS ORPHANED.
#    The TA renames its sourcetype to LOWERCASE `xmlwineventlog`.
#    Splunk_TA_windows renames every other Windows channel to CAPITAL
#    `XmlWinEventLog`. props.conf stanza matching is case-sensitive and nothing
#    defines [xmlwineventlog], so no extraction fired at all. Splunk `rename`
#    means only the TARGET sourcetype search-time settings apply -- the TA
#    orphaned its own extractions.
#
#    Proof the other path works: index=windows carries 471,118 events on
#    sourcetype XmlWinEventLog with EventCode populated. Redirecting the rename
#    there took EventCode from empty to 412,273 ProcessCreate + 9,353 DnsQuery.
#
# 2. THE TA KEYS EVERYTHING ON A SOURCE WE DO NOT PRODUCE.
#    All of its real work lives in
#    [source::XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational].
#    Our UF input is [WinEventLog://...] with renderXml, which yields source
#    `WinEventLog:...` -- no Xml prefix -- so that stanza never matched either.
#    Changing the input to [XmlWinEventLog://...] was TRIED on pp-bp-wkstn-1
#    and did NOT change the source. The host was reverted. Do not re-attempt.
#
# WHY A source:: STANZA. Source stanzas are immune to sourcetype renames, scope
# to Sysmon alone so nothing bleeds onto other Windows channels, and outrank
# sourcetype stanzas in Splunk precedence, so these beat anything
# Splunk_TA_windows sets for XmlWinEventLog.
#
# WHY ONLY NINE LINES rather than a copy of the TA transforms: the raw fields
# are already extracted generically by Splunk_TA_windows once the rename lands.
# Measured at 100% coverage BEFORE this was written -- CommandLine,
# ParentImage, ParentProcessGuid and ParentProcessId each present on all
# 412,273 ProcessCreate events; Computer and QueryName on all 9,353 DnsQuery
# events. Only the CIM aliases were missing.
#
# NO RESTART REQUIRED. Search-time props are read per search from the knowledge
# bundle. Verified: splunkd had been up 11 hours when the rename took effect.
# This also applies retroactively to every event ALREADY INDEXED -- no reindex,
# no cluster bundle push.
#
# BUT THE BUNDLE TAKES A MINUTE OR TWO TO REACH THE SEARCH PEERS. Search-time
# extraction runs on the indexers, so a check run immediately after this file
# lands reads as FAILED and then passes on the next attempt. That cost a round
# of wrong diagnosis; do not read a zero here as a broken mapping without
# re-running a couple of minutes later.
#
# VERIFIED END TO END, 2026-09-04, against live data:
#   EventCode=1   e=418,903  process=418,903  parent_process_path=418,903
#                            parent_process_guid=418,903  parent_process_id=418,903
#   EventCode=22  e=9,496    src=9,496
#
# ON TA UPGRADE: re-check whether it still renames to lowercase. If upstream
# ever fixes that, the first stanza becomes a no-op and can go; the source::
# stanza is still required while our input form differs from what the TA
# assumes.

[XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational]
rename = XmlWinEventLog

[source::WinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational]
FIELDALIAS-process_path     = Image AS process_path
FIELDALIAS-parent_proc_path = ParentImage AS parent_process_path
FIELDALIAS-parent_proc_guid = ParentProcessGuid AS parent_process_guid
FIELDALIAS-parent_proc_id   = ParentProcessId AS parent_process_id
FIELDALIAS-process_guid_cim = ProcessGuid AS process_guid
FIELDALIAS-user_cim         = User AS user
FIELDALIAS-dest_cim         = Computer AS dest
EVAL-process                = coalesce(CommandLine, Image)
EVAL-src                    = if(EventCode="22", Computer, null())
